WEBVTT

00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:04.625
Your agents are everywhere: terminals, tabs, chats.

00:00:04.900 --> 00:00:07.823
Zana brings them all into one command center.

00:00:10.800 --> 00:00:20.030
Then pick any agent: Claude Code, Codex, OpenCode, and
more, all from one composer. Let's ask for a pricing page.

00:00:21.230 --> 00:00:26.819
The agent writes the page into your project, and
the result opens right beside the conversation.

00:00:26.700 --> 00:00:36.123
For bigger goals, just ask for a Squad. The agent launches it: an
orchestrator plans the work and hands tasks to agents working in parallel.

00:00:37.323 --> 00:00:42.783
Flow view shows how the work hands off, from the
plan to the review, until the Squad is done.

00:00:43.983 --> 00:00:51.605
And Zana is modular: everything beyond the core is a
plugin. Add one from the marketplace, in one click.

00:00:51.487 --> 00:00:56.680
Or install your own, straight from a
folder. Here, our team's GUS plugin.

00:00:56.561 --> 00:01:02.625
And because plugins are just code, an agent
can change them too. Let's add a dashboard.

00:01:03.825 --> 00:01:12.652
It edits the plugin, Zana rebuilds it, and the new Dashboard tab is
live: tickets by status, the sprint countdown, and what's blocked.

00:01:12.533 --> 00:01:17.283
And Zana goes where you go: the same app
on your phone, with Slack on the way.

00:01:18.483 --> 00:01:22.108
That's Zana: every agent, one command center.
